The confocal microscopy images demonstrate the efficient uptake of Nano-11 nanoparticles and co-localization with adsorbed ovalbumin (OVA) by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). While soluble OVA uptake is minimal, Nano-11 (red) is readily internalized, and when OVA (green) is adsorbed to Nano-11, a significantly increased amount of OVA is taken up by the BMDCs and co-localizes with the nanoparticles, illustrating Nano-11's role in enhancing antigen delivery to these immune cells.